# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 242-245 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, 2026-09-25): the betrothed girl's three conditions, the city, the
# breach and the thief, the gate where found, the stones, the warning, the field, the holder and the lier, stoning and strangling (242); the girl exempt from
# death, offering and lashes, the pursuer saved by his life, the savior not the place, "let him be" (243); the rapist and the seducer by the a fortiori three
# times — the bedded, the wood-struck, the divorced betrothed, the adult (244); the man not the minor, the father's fifty, Tyrian silver, he drinks from his pot,
# the orphan, the levir (245). Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(242, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF THERE BE A VIRGIN GIRL BETROTHED TO A MAN" (22:23) — HE IS NOT LIABLE UNTIL SHE IS A GIRL, A VIRGIN, BETROTHED TO A MAN. The head row of piska 242 ({SP_(242, 1, "עד", "שתהא", "נערה", "בתולה", "מארשה", "לאיש")} "until she is a girl, a virgin, betrothed to a man"): THE THREE CONDITIONS of the stoning — age, virginity, betrothal — the cell\'s predicate. Fresh.')
srow(242, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND A MAN FOUND HER IN THE CITY" — HAD SHE NOT GONE OUT IN THE CITY, HE WOULD NOT HAVE MET HER. ({SP_(242, 2, "לא", "היה", "מסתקף", "לה")} "he would not have happened on her"): the city\'s presumption — her going out the ground of "she did not cry" (243:3 unmakes the place as a condition). Fresh.')
srow(242, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE CITY, AND HE LAY WITH HER" — THE BREACH CALLS THE THIEF. ({SP_(242, 3, "שהפרצה", "קוראה", "לגנב")} "that the breach calls the thief"): the proverb of the breach (the English adds "any lying" — in the English alone). Fresh.')
srow(242, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"BRING BOTH OF THEM OUT TO THE GATE OF THAT CITY" (22:24) — THIS IS WHAT WE SAID: THE GATE WHERE THEY WERE FOUND, NOT THE GATE WHERE THEY WERE JUDGED. ({SP_(242, 4, "שער", "שנמצאו", "בו", "ולא", "שער", "שנדונו", "בו")} "the gate where they were found and not the gate where they were judged"): THE PLACE OF EXECUTION — the city of the deed (148\'s rule for the idolater at 17:5); the compile\'s parameter. Fresh.')
srow(242, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND STONE THEM WITH STONES" — MANY? "WITH A STONE" (Leviticus 20:27); ONE? "WITH STONES" — IF THEY DIED NOT BY THE FIRST, LET THEM DIE BY THE SECOND. ({SP_(242, 5, "ימותו", "בשניה")} "let them die by the second"): 240:2\'s rite for the pair (Sifrei Numbers 114). Fresh.')
srow(242, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE GIRL BECAUSE SHE DID NOT CRY OUT" — WHEN IT SAYS "BECAUSE OF THE WORD" — BY A WARNING: TO INCLUDE THE DELIBERATE ONE WARNED BY WITNESSES. ({SP_(242, 6, "על", "פי", "התראה")} "by a warning"; {SP_(242, 6, "בהתרית", "עדים")} "by the witnesses\' warning"): THE WARNING (hatra\'ah) — the capital penalty conditioned on the witnesses\' warning, read from "because of the word" (250:1 the same reading ahead); the compile\'s condition on every stoning cell. Fresh.')
srow(242, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE MAN BECAUSE HE HUMBLED HIS NEIGHBOR\'S WIFE" — WHEN IT SAYS "BECAUSE OF THE WORD" — BY A WARNING. ({SP_(242, 7, "על", "פי", "התריה")} "by a warning"): the man\'s warning as the woman\'s — the condition on both. Fresh.')
srow(242, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY IN THE CITY? IN THE FIELD FROM "IF IN THE FIELD THE MAN FINDS HER" (22:25). ({SP_(242, 8, "בשדה", "מנין")} "in the field — whence?"): the second arm opened. Fresh.')
srow(242, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE LAY WITH HER" — EXCLUDING ONE WHO HOLDS AND ONE WHO LIES: R. JUDAH. ({SP_(242, 9, "פרט", "לשאחד", "מחזיק", "ואחד", "שוכב")} "excluding one holding and one lying"): the accomplice\'s liability a DISPUTED cell (R. Judah excludes the holder from the rapist\'s death). Fresh.')
srow(242, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE MAN WHO LAY WITH HER ALONE DIES" — THE FIRST BY STONING, THE SECOND BY STRANGLING. ({SP_(242, 10, "הראשון", "בסקילה", "והשני", "בחנק")} "the first by stoning and the second by strangling"): THE STATUS MOVES WITH THE FIRST ACT — the betrothed virgin\'s violator stoned, her next violator strangled as an adulterer (Sanhedrin 7:9 the answer sheet); the compile\'s status change on the girl. Fresh.')
srow(243, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND TO THE GIRL DO NOTHING" (22:26) — THE VERSE EXEMPTS HER FROM DEATH; FROM THE OFFERING TOO? "SIN"; FROM LASHES TOO? "SIN OF DEATH". The head row of piska 243 ({SP_(243, 1, "שפטרה", "הכתוב", "מן", "המיתה")} "that the verse exempted her from death"; {SP_(243, 1, "אף", "מן", "המכות")} "even from the lashes"): THE COERCED EXEMPT from all three — death, offering, lashes — the sanction table\'s three columns cleared. Fresh.')
srow(243, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR AS A MAN RISES AGAINST HIS NEIGHBOR AND MURDERS HIM" — ALL THE COERCED IN THE TORAH ARE EXEMPT, AND THEY ARE SAVED AT THE COST OF LIFE; ONLY THIS? THE PURSUER AFTER HIS FELLOW TO KILL HIM AND AFTER A MALE — "SO IS THIS THING"; EVEN THE PURSUER AFTER A BEAST, THE SABBATH-PROFANER, THE IDOLATER? "THIS" — THIS IS BY STONING AND NOT ALL THESE. ({SP_(243, 2, "שכל", "אנוסים", "שבתורה", "פטורים")} "that all the coerced in the Torah are exempt"; {SP_(243, 2, "ומצילים", "אותם", "בנפשם")} "and they save them at the cost of his life"): THE PURSUER\'S LAW born here — the rescue by the pursuer\'s life for the murderer and the rapist (Sanhedrin 8:7 the answer sheet — the beast, the Sabbath and the idol excluded); the compile\'s new cell on the coerced and the pursuer. Fresh.')
srow(243, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR IN THE FIELD HE FOUND HER" (22:27) — IN THE CITY LIABLE, IN THE FIELD EXEMPT? "THE BETROTHED GIRL CRIED OUT AND NONE SAVED HER" — IF SHE HAS A SAVIOR, CITY OR FIELD, LIABLE; IF NONE, CITY OR FIELD, EXEMPT. ({SP_(243, 3, "בין", "בעיר", "בין", "בשדה", "פטורה")} "whether in the city or in the field — exempt"): THE SAVIOR IS THE CONDITION, NOT THE PLACE — the city and the field the Torah\'s examples (Mekhilta Neziqin 13); the two arms collapse into one predicate. Fresh.')
srow(243, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"SHE CRIED OUT" — EXCLUDING ONE WHO SAID "LET HIM BE": R. JUDAH. ({SP_(243, 4, "פרט", "לשאמרה", "הנח", "לו")} "excluding one who said: let him be"): the consent after the beginning — R. Judah\'s exclusion. Fresh.')
srow(244, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF A MAN FINDS A VIRGIN GIRL" (22:28) — "VIRGIN" HERE AND "VIRGIN" IN THE SEDUCER (Exodus 22:15): IF THE GRAVE RAPIST IS LIABLE ONLY FOR A VIRGIN, THE LIGHT SEDUCER SURELY; OR THE REVERSE; WHY "VIRGIN" IN THE RAPIST? EXCLUDING THE BEDDED, AND THE ONE STRUCK BY WOOD; "NOT BETROTHED" HERE AND THERE — THE BETROTHED AND DIVORCED; SAID TWICE, THAT HE GIVE NEITHER TO HER NOR TO HER FATHER; "GIRL" HERE AND NOT IN THE SEDUCER — "TO THE GIRL\'S FATHER" (22:29), NOT THE ADULT\'S; THE A FORTIORI CANNOT BE REVERSED, FOR "GIRL" IS SAID TWICE. The head row of piska 244 ({SP_(244, 1, "פרט", "לבעולה")} "excluding the bedded"; {SP_(244, 1, "מכת", "עץ", "מנין")} "the one struck by wood — whence?"; {SP_(244, 1, "קל", "וחמר")} "a fortiori"): THE RAPIST AND THE SEDUCER PAIRED BY THREE A FORTIORI ARGUMENTS (I1) with their reversals — the exclusions the parameters (the bedded, the wood-struck, the divorced betrothed, the adult; Ketubot 3:1-4 the answer sheet\'s table); the largest row of the chapter. Fresh.')
srow(244, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE LAY WITH HER" — ANY LYING. ({SP_(244, 2, "כל", "שכיבה")} "any lying"): 241:1\'s clause for the rapist. Fresh.')
srow(244, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY ARE FOUND" — BY WITNESSES. ({SP_(244, 3, "בעדים")} "by witnesses"): the fine on testimony, not confession. Fresh.')
srow(245, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE MAN GIVES" (22:29) — AND NOT THE MINOR. The head row of piska 245 ({SP_(245, 1, "ולא", "הקטן")} "and not the minor"): the rapist\'s age condition (238:1\'s twin). Fresh.')
srow(245, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO LAY WITH HER" — ANY LYING; "TO THE GIRL\'S FATHER" — THAT THEY BE HIS. ({SP_(245, 2, "שיהו", "שלו")} "that they be his"): the fifty the father\'s (238:5\'s twin). Fresh.')
srow(245, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THE GIRL\'S FATHER" — AND NOT TO THE ADULT WOMAN\'S FATHER. ({SP_(245, 3, "ולא", "לאבי", "הבוגרת")} "and not to the adult woman\'s father"): the age parameter again (238:6). Fresh.')
srow(245, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"FIFTY OF SILVER" — TYRIAN SILVER. ({SP_(245, 4, "כסף", "צורי")} "Tyrian silver"): the coin\'s standard for the fifty as for the hundred (238:4). Fresh.')
srow(245, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHE SHALL BE HIS WIFE" — HE DRINKS FROM HIS OWN POT: EVEN LAME, BLIND, SMITTEN WITH BOILS; A LEWD MATTER OR UNFIT TO ENTER ISRAEL — MAY HE KEEP HER? "SHE SHALL BE HIS WIFE" — A WIFE FIT FOR HIM. ({SP_(245, 5, "באשה", "הראויה", "לו")} "a wife fit for him"): 238:8\'s forced marriage and its exception for the rapist (Ketubot 3:5). Fresh.')
srow(245, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"BECAUSE HE HUMBLED HER" — TO INCLUDE THE ORPHAN; HENCE: AN ORPHAN WIDOWED OR DIVORCED — R. ELIEZER SAYS: THE RAPIST IS LIABLE AND THE SEDUCER EXEMPT. ({SP_(245, 6, "לרבות", "את", "היתומה")} "to include the orphan"; {SP_(245, 6, "האונס", "חיב", "והמפתה", "פטור")} "the rapist is liable and the seducer exempt"): THE ORPHAN\'S FINE HER OWN — the rapist pays her, the seducer nothing (Ketubot 3:6 the answer sheet); the fatherless girl a status arm. Fresh.')
srow(245, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE MAY NOT SEND HER AWAY ALL HIS DAYS" — HE SENDS HER TO THE LEVIR. ({SP_(245, 7, "משלחה", "הוא", "ליבם")} "he sends her to the levir"): 238:10\'s close for the rapist\'s wife — the two undivorceable wives released only to the husband\'s brother (25:5); the chapter\'s last row. Fresh.')
